== Ground transport ==

=== Road ===

The airport is connected to the city's road network via the expressway system, with direct access to the city centre via the southern expressway. Journey time by road to the city centre is approximately 25–35 minutes depending on traffic. Taxi, ride-hailing, and private vehicle access is available at the terminal. Short-term and long-term parking is provided in surface car parks adjacent to the terminal.

=== Bus ===

The municipal bus network operates an airport express route connecting the airport to [[Sant Bart Main Station]] and the city centre, with intermediate stops at the major road junctions along the southern corridor. The service provides the primary public transport connection between the airport and the city, complementing the road access.

=== Rail ===

The airport is connected to the national rail network via the '''Aerotren''', an automated people-mover that links the terminal to the nearest station on the [[Great Eastern Line|Great Eastern rail corridor]], approximately 2.2 kilometres to the west. The Aerotren operates every 5 minutes during peak periods and every 10 minutes off-peak, with a journey time of approximately 4 minutes. The interchange station, '''Sant Bart Sud''', is served by [[Rodalies de Sant Bart|Rodalies]] [[Line B (Rodalies de Sant Bart)|Line B]] (Sant Bart → [[Bellpuig]] → comarca limit). From Sant Bart Sud, the journey to [[Sant Bart Main Station|Sant Bart Main Station]] is approximately 8 minutes by Rodalies.

The airport is not currently connected to the [[Metro de Sant Bart]] rapid transit system. A proposed extension of Metro Line 3 from Zona 10 to the airport has been discussed since the 2010s, but no construction date has been announced.

== Noise abatement ==

The airport's location in the northern portion of Zona 8, surrounded by residential development, creates noise abatement challenges. The northern neighbourhoods of Zona 8, which developed after the airport was established, are affected by aircraft noise during takeoff and landing operations. The airport operates a noise abatement programme that restricts night operations between 23:00 and 06:00, with exceptions for emergency and medical flights. Noise preferential routing procedures are in place for departing aircraft to minimise overflight of residential areas.

